00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:24.970
I mean, I said to the clerk of works, I said,

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:29.980
look, I said, I said, if the local paper...

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.330
I've got the brass neck to call me a villain.

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:36.470
I will personally go down there and set fire to their offices.

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:40.530
I mean, bloody do-gooders trying to tell me that a motorway

00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:44.230
will take away the amenities from the general public.

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:46.950
I said, look, if you have your motorway first,

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:50.270
you can get to your bloody beauty spots that much quicker.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:51.950
Hey?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.450
Oh, dear, why not? Why not?

00:21:58.420 --> 00:21:58.940
Amanda?

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.890
There are three drinks on this table.

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:04.960
Have you had company?

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:05.960
Of course not.

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:06.680
Yes, you have.

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.320
That's what it is.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.240
You've had someone in you.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.320
Was it a man?

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.540
Well, what house?

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:11.600
What do you mean?

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:13.750
Because you're my wife, woman.

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:14.310
Is it?

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:17.490
I'm in the bedroom.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:24.230
I trust you, my darling.

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:27.110
It is the fellas I do not trust.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:29.200
Now, just tell me his name.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:38.400
I don't think you're going to have any more trouble with this, Mrs Nietzsche.

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:41.740
I'll send my bill round tomorrow, OK?

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:43.060
Good night to you both.

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:06.620
I search every house, every pub, every dustbin, I get you!

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:42.390
Wolfie!

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:46.620
It's you, Ken.

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:48.180
Where have you been, mate?

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:49.740
I've wasted up half the night for you.

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:51.370
I just got back from Brighton.

00:23:51.550 --> 00:23:52.590
What, you spent the night in Brighton?

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:54.380
No, in Tucker's van.

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:58.260
At about three o'clock this morning, some hooligans nicked it and dropped it in a quagmire

00:23:58.260 --> 00:23:58.940
near Black Rock.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.870
What are you doing?

00:24:04.190 --> 00:24:05.030
I'm packing up, Kenneth.

00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:06.290
I'm getting out, mate.

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:07.560
Why?

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:10.520
Kenneth, I've done some naughty things in my time.

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:12.990
But I've always steered close to the line of...

00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:13.790
Common decency.

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:14.860
If you like, yeah.

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:17.980
But this time, mate, I have got to go.

00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:23.300
Look, Wolfie, no matter what you've done, it's no good running away from it.

00:24:23.300 --> 00:24:24.400
You've got to stay and face it.

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:28.340
And with God's help and the support of your friends, you can overcome anything.

00:24:29.020 --> 00:24:29.980
Ronnie Lynch caught me in his...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:40.840
bedroom with Mandy. I'll get your socks. Okay. Home, Foxy. I think so, Mrs. J., yeah. Oh, good.

00:24:44.540 --> 00:24:49.840
Mr. Lynch called round last night and again early this morning. Did he have his, uh,

00:24:50.020 --> 00:24:54.900
two friends with him? Oh, no. Oh, thank God. There was about five of them.

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:05.420
Oh, here, Smudge, there's a nasty rumour going about that Lynch has put a contract out on you.

00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:05.720
Yeah.

00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:06.700
For six grand.

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:09.400
Six grand.

00:25:10.350 --> 00:25:12.230
Whoa, that's not bad, is it?

00:25:12.410 --> 00:25:12.590
Phew.

00:25:13.270 --> 00:25:15.540
I just think I could commit suicide and buy a jag.

00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:19.530
Here, talking of jag, somebody's nicked my van.

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:22.350
Don't worry, Tuck, it's in a swamp down in Brighton.

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:23.570
What's it doing there?

00:25:23.890 --> 00:25:24.750
Sinking, slowly.

00:25:25.470 --> 00:25:28.030
Look, I ain't got time to worry about your soppy little van.

00:25:28.130 --> 00:25:28.990
I've got to make tracks.

00:25:29.410 --> 00:25:29.790
Hiya.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.380
somewhere, Foxy? Yes, Mrs. J, I'm leaving. What, for good? No, I'll be back. Ten, eleven

00:25:35.380 --> 00:25:42.170
years' time. Oh, well, I'll keep your bed-haired. Would you like a breakfast before you leave?

00:25:42.390 --> 00:25:49.650
Mrs. J, I've got about four minutes to live. Four minutes? Can boil you an egg? What's

00:25:52.330 --> 00:25:58.750
this all about? Wolfie got caught in a bedroom with Mandy. Did you? No, and that's what hurts.

00:25:59.230 --> 00:25:59.710
Yes.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.680
Six thousand pounds. Not for a lot of money, ain't it?

00:26:04.700 --> 00:26:06.350
Oh, my. Oh, my God.

00:26:06.450 --> 00:26:10.110
Now, look, Wolfie, look, you don't have to go. You'll be all right. You've always survived in the past.

00:26:10.230 --> 00:26:13.230
I've never had a six grand contract out on me in the past, have I?

00:26:13.510 --> 00:26:17.060
I mean, look at the light in his eyes. Listen to the greed in his voice.

00:26:17.500 --> 00:26:19.040
Any minute now, he'll get rich quick.

00:26:19.690 --> 00:26:23.830
Listen, Ken, if I stay, Ronnie Lynch will do a fending on me.

00:26:23.990 --> 00:26:27.510
Yeah, yeah, he'll take me for a midnight dip three miles off Lizard Point.

00:26:27.830 --> 00:26:28.730
But you can swim.

00:26:28.910 --> 00:26:29.890
Not with a lawnmower type.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:35.670
to me left foot, I can't. Where are you going to, Smithy? Out there amongst my people, Tucker.

00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:40.640
I'll be out there where the wind caresses the sea, where the sun burns the earth. Out there

00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:49.770
where the rainbow finally ends. I'll write to you, Smithy. Good lad. Listen, lads, I want

00:26:49.770 --> 00:26:56.680
you all to know that Wolfie Smith, your leader, the Iron Man of Tootin, is not retreating.

00:26:56.780 --> 00:26:59.780
He is not retreating. Right? I am meaning-making.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:07.870
a tactical withdrawal, ready to return fourfold in strength and conviction, ready to wipe

00:27:07.870 --> 00:27:11.540
away corruption, and raise to the ground the temples of capitalism.

00:27:11.740 --> 00:27:16.060
Oh yes, I will walk from my beloved manor with the pride of one who has been chosen.

00:27:16.300 --> 00:27:21.720
I shall not lower my eyes in the shadows of fear, nor whistle a happy tune.

00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:27.190
Instead, I shall walk tall, with dignity, as only a true leader can.

00:27:30.760 --> 00:27:31.340
You
